on>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pi-horizontal-group-item pi-data-value pi-font pi-border-color pi-item-spacing\" data-source=\"bestloot\"><span class=\"no-pseudoelements-container\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><img alt=\"Nightmare Blade\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"32\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Nightmare_Blade_5a1570.gif\" width=\"32\"/></span></span></td>\n<td class=\"pi-horizontal-group-item pi-data-value pi-font pi-border-color pi-item-spacing\" data-source=\"bestloot2\"><span class=\"no-pseudoelements-container\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"#/wiki/Boots%20of%20Haste\"><img alt=\"Boots of Haste\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"32\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Boots_of_Haste_d4312e.gif\" width=\"32\"/></a></span></span></td>\n<td class=\"pi-horizontal-group-item pi-data-value pi-font pi-border-color pi-item-spacing\" data-source=\"bestloot3\"><span class=\"no-pseudoelements-container\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><img alt=\"Wooden Spellbook\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"32\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Wooden_Spellbook_c8e514.gif\" width=\"32\"/></span></span></td>\n<td class=\"pi-horizontal-group-item pi-data-value pi-font pi-border-color pi-item-spacing\" data-source=\"bestloot4\"><span class=\"no-pseudoelements-container\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><img alt=\"Carrot on a Stick\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"32\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Carrot_on_a_Stick_723049.gif\" width=\"32\"/></span></span></td>\n<td class=\"pi-horizontal-group-item pi-data-value pi-font pi-border-color pi-item-spacing\" data-source=\"bestloot5\"><span class=\"no-pseudoelements-container\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"#/wiki/Mandrake\"><img alt=\"Mandrake\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"32\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Mandrake_c4b258.gif\" width=\"32\"/></a></span></span></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Other Properties</h2>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"implemented\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Version</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><span class=\"implementation-date\">11.40.5409<br/>July 25, 2017<br/>Summer Update 2017</span></div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><p>\t    See also: Hunting Places <span class=\"explained\">Help</span></p></nav>\n</aside>\n<p><br/>\nThe <b>Feyrist Meadows</b> is a good place for medium level Mages and <a href=\"#/wiki/Paladin\">Paladins</a> to hunt, specially if the unique items dropped by the creatures on this location (such as the Dream Blossom Staff, the Wooden Spellbook and the <a href=\"#/wiki/Butterfly%20Ring\">Butterfly Ring</a>) have a good price on The Market. It's not a very good place for <a href=\"#/wiki/Knight\">Knights</a> because some of the creatures run from the characters and can make the hunt less efficient and more dangerous. Access to the peninsula is gained through the Troubled Animals mission of <a href=\"#/quest/threatened-dreams-quest\">Threatened Dreams Quest</a>. \n</p><p>The creatures on the surface change depending if it's day or night, and those from the night are slightly stronger and more dangerous. A <a href=\"#/wiki/Dwarven%20Ring\">Dwarven Ring</a> is recommended when hunting here because many of the creatures will get you Drunk.\n</p><p>Besides the creatures on the surface, you will also find dark Fey in three caves (<a class=\"coord-link\" data-coord=\"33492,32291,7\" title=\"Ver no mapa\">south (33492, 32291, 7)</a>, <a class=\"coord-link\" data-coord=\"33424,32215,7\" title=\"Ver no mapa\">west (33424, 32215, 7)</a> and <a class=\"coord-link\" data-coord=\"33554,32211,7\" title=\"Ver no mapa\">east (33554, 32211, 7)</a>), the eastern one being the only big enough for a proper hunt. Also, just south of the lake, there's an entrance to a cave with nightmare creatures by the mountain. This place is more dangerous than the surface, but can also be very good to make some profit. These creatures can also be found on the surface level on the southern side of the mountain, on the path to the <a href=\"#/wiki/Fire%20Shrine\">Fire Shrine</a>. \n</p><p>The Nightmare Creatures cave and peninsula beyond the mountains are a good place for Knights and Paladins to hunt, since the creatures there drop valuable loot more often than others of similar power level. Mages would be wise to avoid these while solo until higher levels, as the creatures there can use <a href=\"#/wiki/Mana%20Drain\">Mana Drain</a> and reduce your Magic Level temporarily.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"w-Teleport_to_Feyrist\">Teleport to Feyrist</span></h2>\n<p>In order to get to peninsula you have to use corresponding gem on <a href=\"#/wiki/Holy%20Shrines\">Holy Shrines</a>, the exact place depends on shrine. You will lose your gem.\n</p><p>Locations of shrines in Feyrist: <a class=\"coord-link\" data-coord=\"33430,32279,7\" title=\"Ver no mapa\">Ice (33430, 32279, 7)</a>,\n<a class=\"coord-link\" data-coord=\"33540,32208,7\" title=\"Ver no mapa\">Earth (33540, 32208, 7)</a>,\n<a class=\"coord-link\" data-coord=\"33587,32262,7\" title=\"Ver no mapa\">Fire (33587, 32262, 7)</a>, and\n<a class=\"coord-link\" data-coord=\"33528,32300,4\" title=\"Ver no mapa\">Energy (33528, 32300, 4)</a>.\nTo go back just use any shrine (does not matter which way you came in) and you will be teleported back.\n</p>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div><table cellspacing=\"0\" class=\"wikitable sortable full-width\"><caption>Surface during Day</caption><tbody><tr><th>Name</th><th data-sort-type=\"number\" style=\"width: 38px; text-align: center;\">Exp</th><t